From e342899cf7263989bd3449b62b33650a86e8624c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TofuJoe <darryl.hon@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:30:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/32] drm/xe: Coalesce full PPGTT TLB invalidations while one
 is in flight

Platforms without range TLB invalidation (e.g. Xe-LP) send every PPGTT
invalidation, one per unbind, to the GuC as a full flush of all TLBs, each
with its own H2G/G2H round trip.

While such a flush is outstanding, reserve one seqno for the next one and
attach later requests to it instead of sending each; send it when nothing
waits on the outstanding one any more (ack, timeout, reset or send error).
Every attached request has finished its page-table update before attaching,
and the merged flush is sent afterwards, so it covers all of them. Any other
invalidation first sends the deferred one to keep seqnos in order.

Disable at runtime with xe.tlb_inval_coalesce=0.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
